From 56a440016140fc8451886af616bcf299c2add735 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:12:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Third review, day-one trust fixes: customer changelog,
 trial terms, Reg 26 badge, pricing for subscribers, OOOO-family intros

- /changelog reads changelog_public() (new migration 20261003160524), an
  aggregate RPC granted to anon: counts by day, regulation and change type,
  no notes, no ids. The page no longer renders provision_changes rows, so the
  pipeline's working log ("Phase 0: regenerated ...", model names, owner
  instructions) and raw change_type values stay in the database. Same page
  logged in or out; the "log in to see the full history" banner is gone.
- Terms of Service: a Free trial paragraph under section 4 (7 days, card
  required, charge at trial end, cancel before to avoid it with access kept
  through the trial, reminder email, one trial per customer, failed charge).
  Last updated October 3, 2026.
- Jurisdiction badge follows the document, not the row: Regulation 26's
  incorporated Subpart JJJJ rows (jurisdiction_level 'federal') now read
  "Colorado" with an "Incorporated federal text" tag on Ask cards. Helpers
  moved to regulation-names.ts so the test can import them without
  server-only.
- /pricing for a subscriber shows the two plans read-only with their own
  marked, instead of redirecting to the Colorado catalog.
- Storage-tank and pneumatic-controller question-map intros name OOOO,
  OOOOa, OOOOb and OOOOc by date window and state-plan status instead of a
  two-way OOOOb/OOOOc split.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
